  "finalText": "I built the 8-second kinetic quote in **Main**: four phrases, each with its own moment, and the attribution last.\n\n- **Phrase 1** \"Design is not just\" (light, 88 px) slides in word by word, then rolls up as phrase 2 comes in.\n- **Phrase 2** \"what it looks like.\" is grey, same word-by-word roll.\n- **Phrase 3** \"Design is\" (light) is a short beat before the hero.\n- **Phrase 4** \"how it works.\" is the hero: 128 px, heavy weight, red (#FF3D2E). It slides in word by word with a slight scale-up, then a red underline wipes in from the left with a small overshoot.\n- **Attribution** \"— Steve Jobs\" (28 px, grey) fades up last at 7.0 s.\n\nEvery phrase exits upward just before the next one arrives, so the text never collides. Ease is Expo Out on entrances and Expo In on exits, throughout.\n\nThe critic scores it 55/100, and the main flag is reading time: phrase 3 is on screen for about one second and phrases 1 and 2 are a little under the 1.4 s it wants for four words. Fixing that means either a longer comp (10 s would give every phrase full reading time) or trimming the words. I left it at 8 s to match the comp you set. Tell me if you want 10 s and I'll re-time it."
